title: Begin
---
You: Good afternoon. Where to, sir?
???: There are two places I need to be at, take me there.

You: Ok, where should we go first?
???: You decide.
===

title: WhereTo
---
???: So, where did you decide to take me?
You: Uhm... I'm just travelling to a marker you gave me, I don't know what awaits at the destination.
???: How is it possible that a cab driver does not know the map.
You: I am the first person to be assigned to this area after the conflict, I am supposed to re-create the map of the area. They pay a hefty sum for this.
???: Why are you doing this job?
    -> Why would I not! They're paying well for the map.
        ???: The money, why do you need it?
    -> I don't know. It's like the rest of my life doesn't matter anymore. I am here now, that is all I know and ever will know, sir.
        ???: Don't worry, this is definitely somewhere to be.
        ???: I believe it was never our destiny to find our purpose in life. But rather to never stop searching.
        ???: Along that journey, this cab, this void in your soul might be all you have, but it's still something.
        ???: Stay the course.
        Paul: You can call me Paul, by the way.
    -> I like meeting new people. Like you, good sir.
        Paul: I'd like to know more about you too. By the way, you can call me Paul.
===

title: Bridge
---
Paul: Slow down, we're there.
Paul: To the left, what do you see.
    -> It's beautiful.
        Paul: Good.
    -> Ruins.
        Paul: It has been like that ever since I came to be. Perhaps from a war long ago. Or it's just an unfinished building, who knows, hard to see from here.
        Paul: The point is, who cares, people should learn to stop looking at the unfinished, the damaged. Appreciate the view.
        Paul: Tell me, what else do you see.
    -> The moon.
        Paul: In the afternoon, you can see the sun too.
        Paul: Sky view through the hole of a torn building. Damn poetic. You should definitely bring some girls here.
        -> I'm bi-sexual
            Paul: Okay. Maybe bring a guy sometimes.
        -> I'm homosexual
            Paul: Sure, bring a guy. Whatever makes you happy.
        -> My sexuallity is complicated.
            Paul: Sure. Bring a friend, then. Whoever makes you happy.
    -> That's enough. Let's get going.
